From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timothy Schmidt <timschmidt@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 20:57:54 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] media: qcom: camss: retain every raw route across MSM8226
 system sleep

The MSM8226 system-sleep support kept one raw capture route at a time
and refused to prepare when a second route was streaming. With CSID1
able to power on, two sensors can now stream at once (CSID0 and CSID1
into separate RDI lines of the single VFE), and suspending the system
then failed with -EBUSY from camss_prepare().

Keep the retained buffers and frame sequence in each VFE line instead
of in struct camss. On prepare, collect every streaming RDI line, take
their queue locks in line order, check that each VFE's power and stream
counts are held only by those routes, stop all of them, halt the VFE
once and hold each line's buffers. On complete, restart every retained
route. A PIX route still refuses system sleep.

Assisted-by: LLM [Claude Code]
